From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:20:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net/netmon: offer CGNAT candidates after tunnel registration

LocalAddresses skipped IPv4 addresses in Tailscale's CGNAT allocation
even on a shared LAN, which could leave peers using a relay. With a
registered tunnel name, offer those addresses on other eligible
interfaces as direct endpoint candidates. Keep the IPv4 range check
when no name is registered and keep excluding the Tailscale IPv6 ULA
range.

Change-Id: Ic23d33bce93a8978c28e2e589845f477cd030f28
Signed-off-by: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
---
 net/netmon/interfaces_test.go | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 net/netmon/state.go           |  9 +++------
 2 files changed, 48 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

